Procedure:

1. Check the installed Git version and configure the global username and email.
2. Verify the Git configuration using git config --list.
3. Clone the GitHub repository and navigate to the project directory.
4. Check the current directory, list files, and verify the repository status.
5. Open README.md in Notepad and make the required changes.
6. Stage the modified file using git add README.md.
7. Verify the staged changes using git status.
8. Commit the changes with the message "FIRST CHANGE".
9. Rename the current branch to main and push the changes to GitHub.
10. Set the upstream branch using git push -u origin main.
